{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nCompletion verification for b42a found that the shipped Mode enum, MODE_CAPS mapping, and reconcile-check phase-gate value remain present, but the acceptance criterion over-attributed their direct coverage to test_mode.py and test_advisory_lock.py. The change is already merged; add focused characterization coverage without changing production behavior.\n\n## Approach\n- Extend the existing mode contract suite to pin the complete MODE_CAPS mapping, including RECONCILE_CHECK=0 and every legacy mode cap.\n- Extend the existing ref-backed advisory-lock phase-gate test to write and read the exact reconcile-check value and prove higher modes block while the equal reconcile-check target remains allowed.\n- Keep all old mode values, ordering, caps, and gate storage unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_mode.py directly asserts the complete MODE_CAPS mapping for all five legacy modes.\n- [x] tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py round-trips gated_mode reconcile-check through the real ref backend and proves equal-versus-higher blocking behavior.\n- [x] No production file changes.\n- [x] Focused tests, make lint, and make typecheck pass.\n\n## Compatibility and rollback\nThis is additive characterization coverage only. Reverting the test commit restores the prior coverage level without changing runtime state."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786155655926088001,"uuid":"457d15b0-377f-4813-a45a-26ea8565852f"}